  "observations": "Observation: Limited. The southern route to (9.0, 8.5), a 0.2-second wait, and the eastward crossing to (14.0, 8.5) were safe. Moving north to about (14.0, 7.88) remained active. Waiting there resulted in outcome 'seen' at time 10.29, when R2 was near (14.15, 5.2) facing west; R4 was near (18.01, 10.85) facing west.",
  "failure": "Observation: Detection occurred while waiting at (14.0, 7.88). Hypothesis: This position was not protected by the spine once R2 moved westward, allowing its sight line to reach the player. Short lesson: Do not wait at an unverified cover edge while a patrol approaches.",
  "next": "Next strategy: Replay the proven southern route and timed crossing, but do not wait at (14.0, 7.88). Use short northward moves immediately after reaching the spine's east end, aiming to pass north of the spine before R2 moves close, then turn west toward the exit.",
  "uncertainty": "R2's exact sight range, cone width, and patrol turning points remain unknown. It is also uncertain whether R2 alone caused detection or whether R4 contributed, and whether the proposed rapid northward passage is safe."
}

